    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NidJm7Tzd128tJp4sbpQtK)_\n\n`sp-ai` is out of the startup list in `init.el`. Its git-sourced packages (claude-code, efrit, vulpea-mcp, monet) made Elpaca block in `elpaca-wait`, and it was the slowest module at start (about 12 to 15 s).\n\nNew command `M-x sp-ai-load` (defined in `init.el`): loads `sp-terminal` (the `eat` backend that claude-code waits for), then `sp-ai`, then runs `elpaca-process-queues` so missing packages install. It logs to `*Messages*` through `sp-require-module`.\n\n**Consequence:** the MCP servers (mcp-server-lib, vulpea-mcp, org-mcp) are down until `sp-ai-load` runs, so Claude's MCP calls through `emacs-mcp-stdio.sh` get no answer. A headless daemon that must serve them needs to run `sp-ai-load` after start.\n\nDocs: `sp-ai.org` and `load-order.org` say so; CHANGELOG entry added. Not run in Emacs (none in the container); parentheses of `init.el` checked by script.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBTiUziZidcdSerB8r)_",
